            <ArticleTitle>Left anterior descending coronary artery-right ventricle fistula complicating percutaneous transluminal angioplasty.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>387-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report describes the development of a false aneurysm at the site of percutaneous transluminal angioplasty of the left anterior descending coronary artery. Rupture of the aneurysm resulted in a coronary artery-right ventricle fistula.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
